AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP is many-to-one: net_recv, ipc_recv and db_read all
become the label `untrusted_input`, and which one it was got discarded at
the moment of derivation. So "a request body reached the database" and "a
row read from the database reached the database" were the same fact
downstream -- and on an ORM-backed application the second dominates. All
140 flows on pretix's largest violated claim are database-read to
database-write.

TaintSource and TaintFlowFinding now carry `source_boundary`; each taint
verdict carries a `flow_origins` breakdown keyed by it; each evidence row
carries it for drill-down. Envelope schema 1.2 -> 1.3.

THE LABEL IS DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED, and that is the design. Giving
database reads their own label was the alternative, and it would have been
a SILENT semantic change to every claim already written against
`untrusted_input`: those flows would simply stop matching. Measured, that
would have flipped 3 of 16 violated cohort claims to `confirmed` with
nobody told (all pretix: untrusted-input-no-database, -no-host-fs,
-no-subprocess). Reporting the split instead changes ZERO verdicts and
ZERO evidence rows (270 -> 270), asserted in both directions by the arm's
instrument before measuring -- a run where db_read flows quietly stopped
matching would produce a cleaner-LOOKING number while measuring the
option that was declined. A test pins that a db_read-sourced flow still
matches an untrusted_input claim.

No new vocabulary minted: the distinction already existed as io_boundary's
controlled categories and was being thrown away, so this carries the
existing axis through rather than promoting a new db_at_rest/external one
(ADR-0024 / R1, "the fact already has a home"). `declared` buckets
YAML-declared sources, which have no boundary.

This measurement corrected two of my own earlier claims, and the feature
is what caught them. Both "dropping ORM reads changes zero verdicts" and
its later "correction" (that 7 non-ORM flows remained) came from a
hand-rolled ORM predicate whose read-set omitted exclude, none, annotate
and select_related -- all genuine Django reads. Production classifies 100
of 100 shown rows as db_read where the ad-hoc predicate found 93. Name the
instrument, then verify it is the one production runs (L53).

